{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And strike the dust of the earth.</b> He did not warn Pharaoh concerning this, nor concerning the boils, nor concerning the darkness — for the nine plagues that served as signs and wonders were דצ״ך עד״ש בא״ח (blood, frogs, lice; wild beasts, pestilence, boils; hail, locusts, darkness) alone, since the plague of the firstborn was neither a sign nor a wonder but a punishment, as explained above (Exodus 4:23; 7:4). Now דצ״ך were signs in the two heavy elements, עד״ש were signs in living creatures, and בא״ח were signs in the air; and in each pair He gave warning, while the third was inflicted without warning, as it says: הֵן כָּל אֵלֶּה יִפְעַל אֵל, פַּעֲמַיִם שָׁלוֹשׁ עִם גָּבֶר (Job 33:29)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:50.171456101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}